### YOUR READING:
Michael Joyce, "Siren Shapes: Exploratory and Constructive Hypertexts" 
(1988)

### CORE QUESTION:
What's the difference between using hypertext to EXPLORE existing knowledge 
(like browsing the Web) versus using it to CONSTRUCT new knowledge (like 
building your own networked thoughts)?

And more critically: Why does this distinction matter for T&T research and 
practice?

