## THEORIES SEMINAR: INTERACTIVE PRESENTATION
### Hermeneutics, Deconstruction, Poststructuralism

Today we're exploring five theoretical frameworks through interactive 
pathways. You'll work in groups to navigate readings, discuss provocations, 
and contribute to a collective theoretical artifact.

**Central Tension:**
Constraint-based systems can be:
- DEMOCRATIC (transparent, participatory, appropriable) OR
- CONTROLLING (opaque, extractive, surveilling)

What makes the difference?

**Your Task (90 minutes):**
1. Navigate your group's pathway (25-30 min)
2. Share insights with class (25-30 min)
3. Generate collective document (15-20 min)

**Before You Begin:**

Take 5-7 minutes to free-write on this prompt:
"Think of a time when a rule, constraint, or system helped you create 
something. What made it enabling rather than limiting?"

Please find your way to this <a href="https://drive.proton.me/urls/VEF2HEV2Q0#BtxXl1gNcmIv">shared document</a> and access it with password (text-rotate-x:40)+(text-rotate-y:6)["`text-tech`"].

